# ZenRay Clipboard (19 October 2026)

- Editable native fork of Maccy 2.6.1 at upstream commit dec66013b1a6865608949845e8eabd85cff3fc29. Existing interface, search, keyboard shortcuts, text/images/files, pins and paste actions remain upstream code. MIT license remains in MaccySource/LICENSE. (19 October 2026)
- Installed app: `/Applications/ZenRayClipboard.app`; original `/Applications/Maccy.app` remains installed and its database is preserved. The original process is stopped for the trial. Startup replacement is not yet configured. (19 October 2026)
- Run `Scripts/BuildClipboard.sh`, then `Scripts/UpdateClipboard.sh`. Use `Scripts/UpdateClipboard.sh --preferences` to open settings directly after rebuilding. Do not rerun InstallClipboard.py: it imports the original history only once and refuses overwriting an existing history. (19 October 2026)
- Advanced settings expose releasePreviewsWhenHidden (true), previewMaxPixels (2048, editable from 512 to 4096) and thumbnailScale (2, editable from 1 to 2). Original clipboard content remains full quality. The preview raster is bounded, not the whole application's memory. (19 October 2026)
- History and imported preferences stay private in `/Users/zenray/Library/Application Support/ZenRayClipboard/`; never commit or archive this folder. Fifty live history entries were copied, with all 8,771,088 live content bytes preserved. The original database also contains stale content rows; only the independent copy excludes these orphan rows. (19 October 2026)
- Automatic upstream binary replacement is disabled, so it cannot overwrite the optimizations. Copy works without Accessibility; simulated automatic pasting may require granting the new app Accessibility permission manually. (19 October 2026)
- Memory measurements after launch: 88 MiB at rest, 98 MiB after search and copying, compared with 446 MiB for the original running process immediately before replacement and the user's 490.8 MB earlier reading. These are different process ages; sustained improvement is not yet established. The first populated panel temporarily reached 297 MiB. (19 October 2026)
- `Scripts/PreviewCheck/main.swift` detects source-image retention. Original resize implementation fails before drawing; optimized implementation passes and validates 400-by-300 pixel thumbnail output for a 200-by-150 point target at scale 2. (19 October 2026)
- Spotlight correction: macOS 27 hosts Spotlight in com.apple.campo (Siri AI). This process must remain enabled for Command Space, even when Assistant Enabled is 0. The previous global modelmanagerd disabling advice is suspended because shared services need a separate dependency review. (19 October 2026)
